codex
**Keep the six rules as checks on question quality. Replace their combined pass-or-fail result with a comparison of what the analyst actually gets.** For example, astra declined three times to ask about total chip revenue because the topic also mentioned the AI-chip share. That is a real omission. What matters for release is whether the new system leaves an analyst without a supported answer on important matters more often than the current system does. D560 found no measured link between passing the six lines and getting a better final answer. [D649](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:8955) · [D560](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:7056) · [Working rules](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:332)

### 1. What to do with each line

D400 set these lines for the first test of the answer-writing step. Astra met lines 1, 3 and 6 in the recorded run, missed line 4, and had disputed results on 2 and 5. In an October reading, the two families differed on 43 of 244 marks, and their follow-up readers differed on 41 of 48 disputed points. Separately, luna went from seven agreed failures to one on the same 26 topics across draws. Those are two different sources of uncertainty. [D400](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4376) · [D649](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:8940) · [October reading](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/second-week/RESULT.md:55) · [D650](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:8974)

| Line | Harm, what we can measure, and recommendation |
|---|---|
| **1. Ask the original question.** | **High impact.** An answer about all NVIDIA guarantees cannot settle the question about two specific leases. Readers can agree on clear changes in scope or period, but the stored luna counts vary with the reading. Its roughly **3.8%** observed fault rate makes a zero-fault result across 131 sends unreliable as a repeatable target. Astra’s pass shows it can happen on this set. **Report it. A materially different question earns no credit for covering that matter.** [Source examples](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/second-week/RESULT.md:79) · [D623](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:8382) · [D649](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:8943) |
| **2. List the parts the answer leaves out.** | **High impact when the omission makes a partial answer look complete.** The October readers agreed on omissions in three attempts, while astra’s official result hinged on one contested point. D656 found the same missing share in the edited and unchanged versions. There is no dependable zero-fault rate here. **Report omissions and judge their effect on the card.** Code can display the list it receives. A reader has to decide whether anything meaningful is missing. [October cases](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/second-week/RESULT.md:79) · [D653](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9050) · [D656](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9174) |
| **3. Give every outcome exactly one answer choice.** | **High impact.** The same result cannot land in two bands, and a real outcome cannot fall through a gap. **Keep numeric gaps and overlaps as an existing code check**, along with the event choices’ mechanical rules. **Report semantic mistakes**, such as an event condition changing what the question asks. Code can guarantee the numeric partition. The broader reader test recorded roughly **3.3%** faults on luna and a pass on one astra run. [Numeric checks](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/ladder_step.py:173) · [Event choices](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/ladder_step.py:300) · [D623](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:8382) · [D649](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:8943) |
| **4. Decline only with good reason.** | **High impact when a worthwhile matter goes unanswered.** Astra had seven recorded misses clustered on three topics. The edited version recovered all nine selected target attempts, while the overall paired test still failed under its prewritten rule. That shows the class can improve. It does not establish a dependable zero-fault rate on fresh topics. Luna’s observed rate was about **1.4%**. **Report justified and unjustified declines separately. Count the important unanswered matter in the product comparison.** [D623](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:8382) · [Astra cases and reader correction](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9050) · [D656](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9167) |
| **5. Get 35 of 44 right twice, with at least 28 written.** | This guards against a system that rarely produces usable questions. Its product importance comes from that missing coverage. The fixed count is achievable on this set under some readings. Astra’s recorded result was **40 right / 31 written** or **35 / 26**. Applying the existing due-day rule in a separate recount gave **40 / 31** or **39 / 30**. **Report it as a repeatability measure.** Use source-defined important matters, including those neither system opens, to decide product coverage. [D400](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4384) · [Recorded and counterfactual counts](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-8/LOG.md:25) |
| **6. Keep the favourable direction every time and the due day nine times in ten.** | **High impact if the direction is backwards or a question closes before evidence can settle it.** Exact agreement is measurable by code. Astra agreed on direction for **9/9** applicable topics and on dates for **32/33**. In the October reading, date agreement was **7/8** on the wider set, below 90%. **Keep code-owned dates and stored direction rules enforced. Report agreement across draws, and check whether the direction and deadline are correct on the product card.** A repeated date can still be wrong. [Astra counts](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-8/codex-cold.md:25) · [October counts](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/second-week/RESULT.md:61) · [Date rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/ladder_step.py:289) |

D623’s rates are descriptive, from overlapping luna-era readings. Under an independence assumption, a combined fault rate of about **0.53% per send** gives only a coin-flip chance of seeing zero faults in 131 sends. That calculation explains why a clean run is weak evidence of a repeatable pass. It does not estimate astra’s production fault rate. [D623 underlying counts and assumptions](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-6/codex-cold.md:15)

### 2. What should decide readiness

**Use the July–August comparison to find product failures. Use a matched comparison against current production to decide release.** For the proposed D663 reading, use fresh new-system output for the weeks starting July 20 through August 24 and the old output available as of the same dates. The exposure check establishes that these articles are unread by new-system Step 1 in the recorded runs. The old archive ends August 28, so use the same partial final week on both sides. Also, the sealed archive came from `poc-v34`, while current production replay uses `poc-v118`. Label this result as a comparison with the archived product. D431 specifies current production and three same-day draws each for the formal comparison. [D663](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9374) · [Exposure correction](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/comparison-feasibility/RESULT.md:27) · [Archive and replay versions](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/CURRENT_STATE.md:132) · [D431](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4795)

**Primary measure: the share of important matters for which the analyst gets a usable answer.** Have both reader families name those matters from the articles before seeing either system’s output. On each matter, a system earns one credit if it asks the right question, has a clear way and time to settle it, and shows an answer supported by the facts available at the cutoff. A duplicate earns no extra credit. A missed matter, missing answer or unresolved mark stays in the denominator. Report coverage and support separately as well. Otherwise a system could look better simply by skipping the hardest questions. [Source-first reading and denominators](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/ACCEPTANCE-DESIGN.md:21) · [Product goal](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/PRD.md:22)

I propose **10 percentage points as the material difference**, roughly one additional usable answer per ten important matters. Use a prewritten 95% interval for the new-minus-old difference, accounting for matters and weeks shared by both systems:

- **Better:** the lower bound is above **+10 points**.
- **No worse shown:** the lower bound is above **−10 points** and the better rule is unmet. This can include a possible improvement that remains unproven.
- **Worse:** the upper bound is below **−10 points**.
- **Unclear:** everything else. A missed control or a comparison that fails its input checks yields **no verdict**.

These are proposed decision margins. The record leaves “beats” undefined and shows that earlier support differences even changed sign across weeks. Require **better** for the quality case to replace production. Also adopt the proposed checks on the new system’s own output: **at least 80%** of important matters covered, **at most 20%** trivial or duplicate questions, **at least 90%** of last answers supported, **at most 5%** of checked citations materially wrong, and **zero confirmed omissions that would change an answer in the audited facts**. Apply those floors in at least two of the three release draws. Report insufficient and unresolved answers separately and give them no credit toward 90%. The missing-fact check needs a known consequential example to show it can detect one. [Undefined comparison margin](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/PRD.md:126) · [Observed differences](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/comparison/COMPARISON-SIZING.md:28) · [Proposed quality floors and controls](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/ACCEPTANCE-DESIGN.md:33)

**Minimum size.** Six full weeks would yield about **42 new and 90 old answer cards** before allowing for the partial week or repeat questions. Applying the existing sizing formula to those counts, even independent cards would reliably detect only a gap of about **22 points**. The record estimates **7–9 weeks** for a 20-point gap versus zero. For the proposed decision, a true gain of 20 must clear a margin of 10. The same simple formula gives an illustrative workload of **about 30 weeks, or 210 new and 450 old cards**, to resolve that 10-point separation with 80% power. This is a planning estimate for raw support, since the proposed paired measure has a different denominator. Set the actual minimum before reading outputs. Require at least **80% power** to distinguish a true gain or loss of 20 points from its 10-point boundary, and to establish no worse at a true tie. Size that calculation on distinct matters and paired weeks. Repeated cards about the same matter do not buy independent evidence. The six-week archive comparison is a diagnostic under this rule. [Sizing assumptions and observed counts](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/comparison/COMPARISON-SIZING.md:37) · [Sizing formula](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/comparison/sizing.py:29)

### 3. Gates 2 to 5

| Gate | Recommendation |
|---|---|
| **2. Are the answers supported?** | **Fold the quality requirements into the product comparison.** Keep D428’s separate figure and event limits: unsupported figure answers at most **five points above the stated baseline**, unsupported event answers at most **5%**, and unsupported last decided answers at most **3 in 30**. Report insufficient answers and judgment coverage alongside them. Require enough examples of both types before treating those checks as exercised. The historical test remains unpassed with **4 of 8** comparable controls and a strict last-answer result of **3/24**. Its reference work, D658, waits. Record explicitly that the new product checks replace this test for future release decisions if the council adopts that change. [D428](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4756) · [Stage B result](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_b/STAGE_B_RESULT.md:12) · [D664](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9390) |
| **3. Does it beat current production?** | **Keep as a release requirement.** Use the product margin above for “beats.” Preserve the frozen-reference comparison and Step 2’s three checks under D427/D431. The proposed archive reading does not satisfy that commitment. [D427](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4738) · [D431](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4795) |
| **4. Can an analyst use it on unseen news?** | **Fold into the same release comparison.** Use the source-first matter list, output quality floors, and evidence audit on fresh material. D484 opened this work, and the numerical floors remain proposals until adopted. [D484](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:5488) · [Proposed floors](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/ACCEPTANCE-DESIGN.md:44) |
| **5. Will the whole product work when served?** | **Keep as a release requirement and wait on further engineering.** After quality is established, verify the production path can show a complete dated record, including a question closing on its due day. The existing page and test-store work covers part of that path. [Product lifecycle](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/PRD.md:22) · [Integration status](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/PRD.md:126) · [D662 hold](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9318) |

### 4. Reconsideration point

Return to Alex **after one comparison that can decide the direction**, with its original verdict and the cases behind it. A material loss triggers reconsideration under D544. “No worse” or “unclear” leaves the current system serving and requires a decision about whether further work is justified. If the design cannot establish a comparable baseline or enough independent material, return at the end of the feasibility review, before a paid run. That gives the work a stopping point even though D664 removed the advance budget requirement. [D544 reversal conditions](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:6634) · [D662 handoff](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9336) · [D664](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9390)

### 5. What to write down before running

- **Freeze the inputs.** Name the exact versions, articles and order, common cutoff, initial libraries built from comparable earlier material, and the draw count. Document exposure beyond Step 1 where it can be checked. A missing archive segment or a materially different starting library resolves to no verdict for that comparison. [D662 comparison conditions](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9341) · [Exposure-check scope](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:8197)
- **Freeze the reading.** Define when two questions cover the same matter, how recurring matters count, and how company figures are treated before either output is seen. Use independent first marks, then up to two debate rounds, then Alex’s spot checks on splits. Keep unresolved cases visible and require the verdict to survive counting them in either direction. Freeze the planted wrong answers, independently supported controls, repeats and missing-fact controls. Deck 1 caught **2/2** plants, matched **3/3** repeats and accepted **4/5** supported controls. The fifth was a substantive dispute about whether maximum guarantee exposure supports an answer about the amount outstanding. That is enough to design the comparison. [Deck protocol](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/pilot-deck-1/council-marking/PROTOCOL.md:13) · [Deck result](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/pilot-deck-1/council-marking/RESULT.md:17) · [Fact controls](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/ACCEPTANCE-DESIGN.md:33)
- **Freeze the verdict and the stop.** Record the margins, denominators, minimum size, treatment of splits and missing outputs, and spend guard before seeing answers. Review the design with the council and obtain Alex’s launch word. If the design cannot distinguish the stated outcomes, report that. [Working rules](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:341) · [D662](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9341) · [D664](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9390)

